-HAMU MASTER — START HERE
+HAMU MASTER V24 — START HERE
 
-1. Double-click start.bat.
-2. It keeps the fixed local port at 3003 (http://localhost:3003), starts the Node server automatically, waits briefly for /health, and opens the lobby in your default browser.
-3. No manual CMD, npm install, or npm start is required. The launcher starts the server in its own child CMD with the admin credential environment inherited reliably. If ws is missing, start.bat installs dependencies automatically.
-4. Admin login: name Samphor. The configured admin credential is provisioned by start.bat and no first-run password prompt is shown.
-5. Existing account/private data is preserved. The launcher never deletes or resets the data directory.
+WINDOWS: Double-click start.bat.
+- Requires Node.js 20+ with npm.
+- Installs the game dependency if missing.
+- Runs on http://localhost:3003 and opens the browser only after successful startup.
+- Keep the server window OPEN while playing. Press Ctrl+C to stop safely.
+- A startup error stays visible; the launcher no longer force-kills Node processes or hides its server in the background.
 
-IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTE
-The requested fixed admin password is supplied by the launcher through HM_ADMIN_PASSWORD. Keep this project folder private because anyone who can read the BAT can see that credential.
+COMMAND PROMPT: npm install, then npm start.
+- npm start defaults to http://localhost:3000 (or your PORT environment setting).
+- Open the address printed by the server. Use one server/start method at a time.
+
+EXISTING ACCOUNTS
+No account files are deleted or reset. Keep the private HamuMaster data folder and any HAMU_DATA_DIR setting unchanged.
+The login/register fix from V23 is included.
+See WINDOWS-START-FIX-V24.txt if startup reports an account-store lock.
+
+SECURITY
+The existing admin configuration remains unchanged. The launcher contains an admin credential, so keep this folder private.
